  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Tidwell held them to two runs through five innings. The Giants mustered two hits and nine strikeouts, never led once, and lost by three.",
    "what_this_means": "Nine strikeouts in a loss tells you everything. The pitching held the door open. Tidwell gave them a window with two earned runs across five innings. But the lineup walked through it and found nothing on the other side. This is a team that has spent the season inconsistent, and today inconsistency looked like a starter who earned a win he never got. Blade Tidwell threw strikes and got outs. The bats stayed silent until it was too late. This is what happens when the formula splits: one part holds and the other part doesn't show. You don't lose games like this by accident.",
